  "description": "BEMNUD crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group A e a 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H46 Ce3 Mn2 N6 O28,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.237-3.811 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.55-109.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C36H46Ce3Mn2N6O28·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
